         "explain": "## Step 1: CRP is slow but useful over time\n\n>> CRP **lags 12–24 h** — a normal CRP early does NOT exclude sepsis.\n\nIts real value is the **trend**: rising/falling CRP guides how long to treat.\n\n## Step 2: Procalcitonin is faster\n\n>> Procalcitonin **rises quicker, peaks higher, falls quicker** — but is unreliable in the **first 1–3 days** of life (naturally high).\n\n## Step 3: Use them together\n\n>> Add procalcitonin when the baby looks septic but **CRP is normal** — it can catch what CRP has not yet shown.",
