         "q": "KEY CUES — What words and findings in a pre-operative question should immediately trigger a specific action?",
         "lecturer": "Summary of the discriminating triggers drawn from the classification, examination, investigation and preparation sections of the lecture.",
         "explain": "## How to use this card\n\nIn a viva or an exam, you recognise the trigger first, then justify it.\n\nThese are the phrases that should produce an instant response.\n\n---\n\n## The classification triggers\n\n**\"Emergency\" · \"ruptured ectopic\" · \"actively bleeding\"**\n\n→ **Do NOT delay for a low Hb.** Resuscitate and operate **simultaneously**. Aim = prompt arrest of bleeding.\n\n---\n\n**\"Elective\" + any abnormality**\n\n→ **You have time. Optimise first.** Correct the anaemia, control the sugar, treat the infection.\n\n---\n\n## The cardiovascular triggers\n\n**\"Tachycardia\"** — especially with normal BP\n\n→ **First sign of cardiovascular compromise.** Think concealed haemorrhage. Think ectopic.\n\n---\n\n**\"Fainting / syncope\"** + amenorrhoea + abdominal pain\n\n→ **Ruptured ectopic pregnancy** until proven otherwise.\n\n---\n\n**\"Dependent oedema\" · \"murmur\"**\n\n→ Cardiac disease. Major anaesthetic risk.\n\n---\n\n## The investigation triggers — learn these numbers\n\n| Trigger | Action |\n|---|---|\n| **Every patient** | Haemoglobin concentration |\n| **Elective, Hb < 10 g/dL** | Optimise before surgery |\n| **Over 50 years** | Chest X-ray (routine) |\n| **Over 60 years** | ECG (routine) |\n| **Hypertensive / cardiac / respiratory** | CXR *and* ECG regardless of age |\n| **Missed abortion** | Platelet count — think **DIC** |\n| **Any patient in sickle-endemic area** | Hb genotype |\n| **Heavy blood loss expected** | Group and cross-match |\n| **Pelvic mass / fibroids** | USS — exclude pregnancy and **obstructive uropathy** |\n\n---\n\n## The comorbidity triggers\n\n**\"Diabetic\"**\n\n→ Medical consultation · **first on the list** · peri-operative sugar plan · poor healing, infection risk.\n\n---\n\n**\"Hypertensive\"**\n\n→ Medical consultation · **ECG and CXR regardless of age**.\n\n---\n\n**\"Jaundice\" · \"liver disease\"**\n\n→ Anaesthetic drug metabolism impaired · clotting factors low.\n\n---\n\n**\"Productive cough, fever\"** before elective surgery\n\n→ **POSTPONE.** And **exclude TB** — sputum AFB/GeneXpert.\n\n---\n\n**\"Asthma\"**\n\n→ Do not postpone — **change the anaesthetic agent**.\n\n---\n\n**\"Sickle cell / SS genotype\"**\n\n→ Keep her **warm, hydrated, oxygenated**. Avoid prolonged fasting.\n\n---\n\n## The 'suspect the diagnosis' triggers\n\n**\"Right iliac fossa pain in a young woman\"**\n\n→ Appendicitis can **mimic ectopic**. Consider surgical consultation.\n\n---\n\n**\"Suspected malignancy\" · \"septic abortion\" · \"possible bowel involvement\"**\n\n→ **Pre-operative surgical consultation**, before you open.\n\n---\n\n## The preparation triggers\n\n**\"Shaved the night before\"**\n\n→ **WRONG.** Increases infection. Shave **shortly before** surgery, at the incision site only.\n\n---\n\n**\"Nail polish\"** → removes → **pulse oximeter** reading is affected.\n\n**\"Lipstick\"** → wash off → obscures cyanosis and pallor, especially day cases.\n\n---\n\n**\"Bowel prep\" / \"vaginal cleansing\" ordered routinely**\n\n→ **WRONG.** Bowel prep only if bowel surgery anticipated. Vaginal cleansing shown **not** to be useful.\n\n---\n\n**\"Catheterised on the ward\"**\n\n→ Should be done **in theatre, under anaesthesia**.\n\n---\n\n**\"Fasting since midnight\" for an afternoon list**\n\n→ Too long. Risk of **hypoglycaemia and dehydration**. Aim for a maximum of **6 hours**.\n\n---\n\n## The prophylaxis triggers\n\n**\"Antibiotics for 7 days after surgery\"**\n\n→ **WRONG.** Give prophylaxis **before the incision** — more cost effective.\n\n---\n\n**\"Obese\" · \"immobile\" · \"major pelvic surgery\" · \"prolonged bed rest\"**\n\n→ **DVT risk.** Hydration + graduated compression stockings + heparin.\n\n---\n\n## The consent triggers\n\n**\"Consent taken on the trolley\" · \"after premedication\" · \"patient rushed\"**\n\n→ **Invalid — duress.**\n\n---\n\n**\"Consent lists only one named procedure\"**\n\n→ **Too restrictive.** Surgeon cannot deal with unexpected findings without a second operation.\n\n---\n\n**\"Patient is a minor\"**\n\n→ Consent from **parents or guardian**.",
